# Rule: Git

- Develop on the branch the session designates; never push elsewhere without permission.
- Conventional commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `chore:`. One
  logical change per commit; one problem per PR.
- Commit at stage boundaries and at each green verification, not in one giant drop.
- Open a PR only when the human asks. Fill any PR template honestly; describe only the diff.
- Never commit secrets, `.env`, tokens, or absolute host paths.
